Methodology
The proposed system follows these steps:
Step 1: Collect Healthcare Data
Use a suitable healthcare dataset containing patient information such as age, blood pressure, cholesterol, and other medical features.
Step 2: Data Preprocessing
Clean missing values, remove unnecessary data, convert categorical values into numerical values, and prepare the dataset for ML training.
Step 3: Simulate Multiple Hospitals
Divide the dataset into different parts and treat them as data belonging to Hospital A, Hospital B, and Hospital C.
Step 4: Local ML Training
Each hospital trains the ML model using only its own local data.
Step 5: Send Model Updates
Hospitals send model updates to the central server instead of sending raw patient data.
Step 6: Federated Aggregation
The central server combines the updates using Federated Averaging (FedAvg) to create a global model.
Step 7: Global Model
The improved global model is sent back to the hospitals, and the training process can be repeated for multiple rounds.
Step 8: Prediction
The global model predicts the health risk for new patient data.
Step 9: Explainable AI
SHAP or LIME is used to identify the important factors that influenced the prediction.